hifiberry-audiocontrol (0.8.8) trixie; urgency=medium

  Player definitions have moved out of /etc/audiocontrol/audiocontrol.json into
  /etc/audiocontrol/players.d/, one file per package that provides a player.
  The players array is removed from an existing audiocontrol.json on upgrade; a
  copy of the previous file is left as audiocontrol.json.bak.

  Two consequences:

  * A player you disabled with "enable": false in audiocontrol.json becomes
    enabled again, because that entry is removed and the package default
    applies. Re-apply the setting in the matching file under
    /etc/audiocontrol/players.d/. This is most visible for librespot, which
    reappears as a Spotify Connect endpoint on the network.

  * Devices where /etc/audiocontrol/players.d/ files were created by hand will
    see conffile prompts for librespot.json and shairport.json, whose packaged
    content differs from the hand-written version. Accept the packaged version
    unless you deliberately changed it.

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Mon, 03 Aug 2026 13:24:53 +0000
